  {
    "expand": "renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations",
    "id": "10242",
    "self": "https://simeoncalixte1990.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10242",
    "key": "AIN-13",
    "fields": {
      "summary": "[Bug][Finance] Repair the failing pipeline parity gate before financial releases",
      "description": {
        "type": "doc",
        "version": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Finance completion audit \u2014 2026-11-01. Planning priority P0. Evidence classification: command-reproduced-previous-review."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Observed behavior / current model"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "npm run pipeline:verify failed in the preceding review: runtime body differences and missing EnsuredPipelineSchemaGeneration/src/pipeline/schemaGeneration/catalogAssembly.ts; scripts/verify-pipeline-parity.mjs reads the stale target."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Required change / expected behavior"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Reconcile package ownership and parity manifests without deleting meaningful verification."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Acceptance criteria"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "bulletList",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Clean checkout pipeline:verify completes successfully."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "CI verifies the actual versions of compute, capacity and shared financial models."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Verification and boundaries"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Review covers the local working tree, which includes uncommitted changes. No production data or live payment provider was modified or validated. Gap tickets represent missing capability, policy or verification, not a claim of an exploited defect. Preserve immutable financial evidence, tenant isolation and existing working flows."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Single-developer sprint sequence \u2014 2026-11-04"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Target candidate: AIN S01 | Build and paid-access guardrails (Jira sprint 36)."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Sprint outcome: Make the clean-checkout verification reliable and close the two bounded production checkout guardrail defects."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Exit evidence: Pipeline parity passes; unconfigured paid production checkout and unauthorized plan selection are rejected with regression evidence. Existing active sprint dates stay unchanged."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Planning envelope: 6 implementation days + 2 integrated verification days + 1 review/refinement day + 1 contingency day; not measured velocity. One primary outcome in progress; at most two closely related workflow slices. Story/task pairs share effort, not double-counted work."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Existing active sprint remains active with original dates; only its goal/name and unfinished membership are reorganized. Every new sprint is future and undated. No fabricated story-point/time estimates or assignees. The ordered slots are a provisional work breakdown, not a fixed delivery forecast. Before activation, split any candidate exceeding six implementation days and verify reviewer/provider readiness; preserve all parent acceptance criteria."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Scheduling is not implementation: original AC/DoD and parent scope are unchanged. Related story/task/subtask effort is one delivery slice, not additive capacity. Required domain slices can be delivered earlier than the broader owner completion sprint; no broader item is Done until all original requirements pass."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
